From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:12:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] DPP: Require a PMKSA of the DPP AKM before skipping Network Introduction

wpas_dpp_check_connect() skips Network Introduction if
wpa_sm_pmksa_exists() finds a PMKSA for the BSS. That lookup ignores the
AKM, so a PMKSA from an SAE association, made while the AP did not offer
the DPP AKM, counts for DPP. When the AP offers DPP again, the station
associates with the DPP AKM without a PMKID, and the AP rejects the
Association Request with status code 53 (invalid PMKID). The DPP check
in BSS selection uses the same lookup, so such a PMKSA also makes a BSS
selectable for a DPP network without a Connector.

Look up a PMKSA of the DPP AKM instead, in both places. For an MLO
association, also require the entry under the AP MLD address, which the
association uses. Decide on MLO with the condition that
wpas_populate_assoc_ies() and sme_send_authentication() use, since
bss->mld_addr is set for every BSS of an AP MLD, also when the station
does not support MLO.

BSS selection now accepts a BSS without the DPP AKM, as
wpas_dpp_check_connect() does. It does not check the partner links of
an AP MLD, since an MLO association uses the PMKSA of the AP MLD.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/wpa_supplicant/bss.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/bss.c
@@ -2016,6 +2016,29 @@
 
 
 /**
+ * wpa_bss_assoc_mld_addr - Get the AP MLD address of an association
+ * @wpa_s: Pointer to wpa_supplicant data
+ * @bss: BSS table entry
+ * @ssid: Target SSID (or %NULL)
+ * Returns: The AP MLD address, or %NULL if an association with the BSS does
+ * not use MLO
+ */
+const u8 * wpa_bss_assoc_mld_addr(struct wpa_supplicant *wpa_s,
+				  struct wpa_bss *bss, struct wpa_ssid *ssid)
+{
+	if (!(wpa_s->drv_flags2 & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS2_MLO) ||
+	    is_zero_ether_addr(bss->mld_addr))
+		return NULL;
+
+	if ((wpa_s->drv_flags & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS_SME) &&
+	    !wpa_bss_get_usable_links(wpa_s, bss, ssid, NULL))
+		return NULL;
+
+	return bss->mld_addr;
+}
+
+
+/**
  * wpa_bss_parse_basic_ml_element - Parse the Basic Multi-Link element
  * @wpa_s: Pointer to wpa_supplicant data
  * @bss: BSS table entry
